ALGORITHM JSP_Request_Response_Flow(request)

BEGIN

    browser SENDS HTTP request TO webServer


    webServer FORWARDS request TO servletContainer


    resource ← MAP_REQUEST_URL(request.URL)


    IF resource is a Servlet THEN

        servlet ← LOAD_SERVLET(resource)


        IF servlet is not initialized THEN

            CALL servlet.init()

        ENDIF


        CALL servlet.service(request, response)

        servlet MAY:

            READ request parameters

            VALIDATE input

            CALL JavaBean/service/DAO

            ACCESS database using JDBC

            STORE result in request/session scope

            FORWARD request TO JSP

    ENDIF


    IF resource is JSP OR request is forwarded to JSP THEN

        IF JSP has not been compiled OR JSP was modified THEN

            TRANSLATE JSP into Servlet source

            COMPILE generated Servlet

            LOAD and INITIALIZE generated Servlet

        ENDIF


        EXECUTE generated JSP Servlet

        READ attributes from request/session/application

        GENERATE dynamic HTML content

    ENDIF


    SET HTTP status and response headers

    SEND generated HTML response TO browser

    browser RENDERS page

END
